  "attribution": "Counts only: ptrace perturbs execution. Timestamps select/merge processes; no elapsed syscall time, latency, throughput, or phase CPU is derived. Subject starts at its successful execve, excluding parent driver preparation and child pre-exec setup. Descendants are linked by successful clone/fork returns translated into the host PID namespace. BusyBox in-process applets need not generate an execve. A wire count is a successful sendmsg/writev with an untruncated first iovec beginning with one full ubus header; it is not an independent receiver acknowledgement. Existing fixture validation proves ordered event acceptance and complete baseline bytes. Unknown tree edges or wire encodings lower attribution completeness, never become zero.",
